WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:03.040
I’m often asked
what my opinion

00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:05.600
about a diet
or disease is.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:11.920
Who cares what my or
anyone else’s opinion is.

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:16.000
All we should care about
is what the science says.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:18.160
What does the best available
balance of evidence

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:20.080
Published in the peer-
reviewed medical literature

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:21.360
have to say right now?

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:24.800
Welcome to the
Nutrition Facts Podcast,

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:27.360
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:31.920
Our story today is about
an alternative approach

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:33.920
to some of the health
problems that bother us.

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:39.120
And we start with the unusual
powers of garden variety lettuce.

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:43.840
There is a perception that time
spent asleep is time wasted,

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:47.600
but it is widely recognized that
inadequate sleep is associated

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:50.160
with multiple acute
and chronic conditions,

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:52.800
and results in the increased
risk of death and disease.

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:57.040
Force people to go one week with
only six hours of sleep a night,

00:00:57.040 --> 00:01:00.320
and you can change expression
of more than 700 genes.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:04.720
The most dire effect may
be endothelial dysfunction.

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:08.720
The endothelium is the thin layer of
cells that covers the internal surface

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:11.760
of blood vessels and is responsible
for allowing our arteries

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:14.640
to relax and dilate
back open properly.

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:18.960
Randomize people for about a week
to get five rather than seven hours

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:22.080
of sleep, and just that two-hour
difference a night resulted

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:26.160
in a significant impairment
in artery function.

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:30.960
Okay, but what do these numbers mean?
How bad is a week of 5-hour nights?

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:33.280
Sleep deprivation is no joke.

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:38.160
The magnitude of impairment is similar
to that reported in people who smoke,

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:41.120
have diabetes, or have
coronary artery disease.

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:44.560
No wonder people who sleep less than
seven hours a night may experience

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:48.000
a 12% to 35% increased
risk of premature death

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:50.080
compared to those who
get a full seven hours.

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:53.120
Yet a significant proportion
of the population may

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:55.120
routinely get less than that.

00:01:55.760 --> 00:01:59.040
Sufficiently long, restful
sleep sessions each night

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:03.280
are said to be an indisputable
cornerstone of good health.

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:05.600
Okay, so what can we do about it?

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:10.000
Those who have sleep apnea,
a common consequence of obesity

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:14.000
that interferes with sleep, benefit
from the use of CPAP machines

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:17.120
while they're losing the weight to treat
the underlying cause, hopefully.

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:20.000
But what if apnea isn't your problem?

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:23.696
What if you just have trouble
falling asleep or staying asleep?

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:28.400
Any natural dietary remedies?
I already have videos on using

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:32.400
kiwifruit to fight insomnia,
and tart cherries, too.

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:34.480
Are there any vegetables
that might help?

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:39.520
Lactuca sativa is a plant that
has been traditionally used

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:40.880
in the treatment of insomnia.

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:45.680
What is this exotic sounding
leafy vegetable? Lettuce!

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:50.720
Evidently lettuce extracts have been
used from the time of the Roman Empire

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:54.240
as agents with sedative and
sleep-inducing properties.

00:02:54.960 --> 00:02:58.960
Lettuce actually does have a hypnotic
substance in it called lactucin,

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:01.920
which is what makes
lettuce taste a little bitter.

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:05.760
But you don't know if it actually
works until you put it to the test.

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:11.600
And it works...in toads.
But it also works in rodents.

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:14.880
Sleep in both mice and rats
is enhanced by romaine lettuce.

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:18.400
They used romaine since
it has a higher lactucin content

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:22.560
compared to other lettuces.
Okay, but does it work in people?

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:26.160
About 10 years ago, a study was
published in which insomnia sufferers

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:30.880
were randomized to receive lettuce seed
oil, oil extracted from lettuce seeds.

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:34.640
Within a week, about 70% of those
in the lettuce seed oil group

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:37.040
said their insomnia very much
or much improved,

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:40.000
compared to only 20% in
the placebo control group.

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:43.840
The researchers concluded that lettuce
seed oil was found to be a useful,

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:48.400
safe sleeping aid in geriatric patients
suffering from sleeping difficulties.

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:52.480
They chose to study older individuals
because insomnia affects surprisingly

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:56.560
20 to 40% of older adults
at least a few nights a month.

00:03:56.560 --> 00:03:59.920
You think that's bad. Sleep
disturbances can plague as many

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:03.120
as nearly 8 out of 10 women
during pregnancy.

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:06.160
Of course, there's lots
of different sleeping pills,

00:04:06.160 --> 00:04:09.120
but they may endanger
the fetus or mother.

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:12.640
For example, doctors frequently
prescribe Ambien for pregnant women

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:16.000
who have trouble sleeping, but Ambien
use is associated with a wide range

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:18.080
of adverse pregnancy outcomes

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:22.080
like low birth weight babies,
premature birth, and cesarean section.

00:04:22.080 --> 00:04:24.560
And the use of valium during
pregnancy has been linked

00:04:24.560 --> 00:04:27.840
to birth defects
including limb deficiencies.

00:04:28.640 --> 00:04:34.000
There has to be a better way.
What about trying lettuce?

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:37.360
The lettuce oil study had
a number of limitations.

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:40.560
For example, it was only single-blind,
meaning the researchers knew

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:43.440
who was on the lettuce supplements
and who was on placebo,

00:04:43.440 --> 00:04:47.040
which could have introduced some bias.
But the researchers essentially said,

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:50.800
"Give us a break. Big pharma
has billions to spend on research.

00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:52.960
No one wants to fund
studies on lettuce."

00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:56.720
Finally, we got a double-blind,
placebo-controlled study,

00:04:56.720 --> 00:05:00.720
but this time on a whole food,
not just a lettuce seed extract.

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:04.400
Yeah, but how to you come
up with a placebo lettuce?

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:07.040
How are you going hide who
gets lettuce and who doesn't?

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:10.240
Well, you can't fit a head
of lettuce into a capsule,

00:05:10.240 --> 00:05:13.360
but you can fit whole
lettuce seeds.

00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:17.520
And here we go: a double-blind
randomized placebo-controlled trial

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:21.360
on lettuce seeds for
pregnancy-related insomnia.

00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:24.080
A hundred pregnant women
with insomnia were randomized

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:27.200
to receive capsules containing
either a quarter teaspoon

00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:30.400
of ground lettuce seeds or
a placebo for two weeks,

00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:33.520
and those on the lettuce seeds
saw a significant improvement

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:35.360
in a sleep quality index score

00:05:35.360 --> 00:05:38.560
compared to placebo
with no reported side effects.

00:05:40.240 --> 00:05:41.520
In our final story today,

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:44.240
we look at how cranberries
and pumpkin seeds

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:46.800
may help with an
enlarged prostate.

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:52.880
More than 50% of men in their 50s
and 70% or more of men in their 60s

00:05:52.880 --> 00:05:56.480
suffer from benign prostatic
hypertrophy or BPH,

00:05:56.480 --> 00:05:58.640
otherwise known
as enlarged prostate.

00:05:59.280 --> 00:06:02.720
This can result in burdensome
lower urinary tract symptoms

00:06:02.720 --> 00:06:06.240
such as having to get up
frequently at night to pee.

00:06:06.240 --> 00:06:09.680
Current medical treatments are
clinically effective, but their efficacy

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:12.960
is compromised by side effects
and low compliance rates.

00:06:12.960 --> 00:06:18.320
Symptoms include sexual dysfunction,
high-grade prostate cancer,

00:06:18.320 --> 00:06:22.080
and depression. No wonder
there's poor compliance.

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:26.160
And when medication treatment fails,
surgical procedures are considered,

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:29.920
such as transurethral
resection of the prostate.

00:06:29.920 --> 00:06:33.920
There has got to be a better way.

00:06:33.920 --> 00:06:36.800
Population studies suggest
that low intake of animal protein

00:06:36.800 --> 00:06:39.600
and high intake of fruits and
vegetables may be protective,

00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:42.720
but not just cutting down
on any animal protein.

00:06:42.720 --> 00:06:47.440
Eggs and poultry seem to be the
worst, along with refined grains,

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:49.920
but no association was found
for red meat or dairy.

00:06:50.480 --> 00:06:54.560
Population studies aside, are there any
foods that have been put to the test?

00:06:55.360 --> 00:06:58.080
There have been more than 30
randomized controlled trials

00:06:58.080 --> 00:07:03.360
on the herb saw palmetto, and it's
been found to be totally useless.

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:07.440
Evidently, cranberries were used
by Native Americans to treat

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:12.560
urinary ailments, but you don't
know until you put 'em to the test.

00:07:13.600 --> 00:07:17.520
Now, when they say dried cranberries,
they're not talking about those sugary,

00:07:17.520 --> 00:07:22.000
oily craisins, but rather just
straight, whole cranberry powder.

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:26.400
And significant improvements were
seen in BPH symptoms, quality of life,

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:28.000
and all urination parameters

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:30.880
for just about a teaspoon a day
of powdered cranberries.

00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:35.280
So we know a teaspoon works,
but what about a third of a teaspoon

00:07:35.280 --> 00:07:38.000
or a sixth of a teaspoon?
They also helped.

00:07:38.240 --> 00:07:40.080
Now this study used a supplement

00:07:40.080 --> 00:07:42.400
because it was funded by
the supplement company,

00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:45.040
but the supplement is just
straight cranberry powder,

00:07:45.040 --> 00:07:48.000
so you might as well buy it
in bulk for much cheaper

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:49.840
and just add it to a
smoothie or something.

00:07:50.480 --> 00:07:52.880
What about using a berry
that's a little tastier,

00:07:52.880 --> 00:07:57.840
like drinking purple grape juice?
No benefit whatsoever.

00:07:58.560 --> 00:08:01.840
In a previous video, I talked
about the use of flaxseeds,

00:08:01.840 --> 00:08:05.200
which may have a therapeutic
efficacy comparable to that

00:08:05.200 --> 00:08:08.880
of commonly used drugs,
with only good side effects.

00:08:08.880 --> 00:08:11.680
Okay, so what about other seeds?

00:08:11.680 --> 00:08:14.480
Pumpkin seeds have evidently
been used in folk medicine

00:08:14.480 --> 00:08:17.520
as a remedy for prostate
disorders for centuries,

00:08:17.520 --> 00:08:21.760
and in a petri dish, they can cut the
growth of BPH prostate cells in half.

00:08:22.400 --> 00:08:26.240
Scientists have also injected
pumpkin seed extracts into rabbits,

00:08:26.240 --> 00:08:28.160
but what about people?

00:08:29.040 --> 00:08:32.080
Pumpkin seed oil appears
to help with prostate issues.

00:08:32.080 --> 00:08:35.200
When pitted head-to-head
against the drug Prazosin,

00:08:35.200 --> 00:08:37.120
it seemed to work
as well as the pill.

00:08:37.120 --> 00:08:40.240
The same when it was head-to-head
against the drug Terazosin.

00:08:40.960 --> 00:08:43.600
What they didn't have though
was a placebo group.

00:08:43.600 --> 00:08:46.400
It would have been nice to see how
well the pumpkin seed oil supplements

00:08:46.400 --> 00:08:50.960
did against placebo, and hey,
in an ideal world, I'd love to also see

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:53.920
a group just given whole
pumpkin seeds themselves,

00:08:53.920 --> 00:08:58.920
and boom: there it is. More than
a thousand men were randomized

00:08:58.920 --> 00:09:02.880
to either a pumpkin seed
extract, a placebo,

00:09:02.880 --> 00:09:05.600
or just about a tablespoon
a day of plain pumpkin seeds.

00:09:06.320 --> 00:09:09.920
The study was funded by the drug
company that made the supplement,

00:09:09.920 --> 00:09:13.280
but the supplement flopped,
it was no better than placebo,

00:09:13.280 --> 00:09:16.320
but the pumpkin seeds
themselves worked.

00:09:16.880 --> 00:09:20.400
The supplement appeared to reduce
symptoms, but not better than placebo.

00:09:20.400 --> 00:09:22.640
However, just the plain old seeds did.

00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:26.240
So it wasn't just some compound
extracted from the oil.

00:09:26.240 --> 00:09:30.800
And, in fact, we've since learned that
even an oil-free extract seemed to work.

00:09:30.800 --> 00:09:34.400
Bottom line, the researchers concluded,
is that pumpkin seed could be

00:09:34.400 --> 00:09:37.760
recommended for BPH patients
with mild-to-moderate symptoms.

00:09:38.320 --> 00:09:42.080
This conclusion was echoed by the
European equivalent of the FDA.

00:09:42.080 --> 00:09:46.160
Pumpkin seeds can be used for the
relief of lower urinary tract symptoms

00:09:46.160 --> 00:09:49.600
related to an enlarged prostate
after more serious conditions

00:09:49.600 --> 00:09:52.257
have been excluded
by a medical doctor.

00:09:53.840 --> 00:09:56.880
